From 0552d34e6b2dd2c220405212ecb73a47e96545ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kkutysllb <46704313+kkutysllb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 22:29:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(llm): tolerate relay API keys in openai-codex accountId
 extraction

The openai-codex-responses stream unconditionally decodes the configured
key as an OpenAI OAuth JWT and hard-fails with "Failed to extract
accountId from token" when the claim is absent. Relay/proxy deployments
configure plain API keys against a custom baseUrl, so every turn died
with PI_AI_ERROR before any request went out.

Add a pnpm patch for @earendil-works/pi-ai@0.84.3: on extraction failure,
fall back to a stable token-derived id instead of throwing. The value
only feeds the chatgpt-account-id header and the WebSocket session cache
key, both meaningless to relays; real OAuth JWTs keep the original path.

Verified: differential probe (non-JWT key: pre-patch accountId error,
post-patch network error against an unreachable baseUrl); vitest
packages/llm/llm-pi-ai 264/264 green.
